<title>UK: Cuba Jan/July sugar exports rise sharply yr/yr-ISO.</title>
<headline>Cuba Jan/July sugar exports rise sharply yr/yr-ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cuba's sugar exports for the first seven months of 1996 amounted to 3.74 million tonnes, sharply up on the same period in 1995 when they totalled 2.57 million, the International Sugar Organization (ISO) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bulk of the exports over the period were destined for Russia, which imported 1.83 million tonnes compared with 699,649 tonnes in January-July 1995, the ISO said.</p>
<p>But sugar exports for July 1996 alone were light at just 70,909 tonnes, less than half the July 1995 figure of 144,753 tonnes, and mainly went into the European Union and China.</p>
<p>Cuba's sugar campaign runs from December to June.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
